  "title": "Kirby Problem 1.48",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "(a) Suppose $K$ and $K\\#J$ are (smoothly) doubly slice knots.\nMust $J$ be a\n(smoothly) doubly slice knot?\n(b) Does there exist a knot that is smoothly slice, topologically doubly slice, and\nnot smoothly doubly slice but such that $K\\#K$ is smoothly doubly slice?\n(c) Let $M$ and $N$ be closed 3-manifolds such that $M$ and $M\\#N$ embed (smoothly)\nin $S^{4}$. Must $N$ embed (smoothly) in $S^{4}$?",
